#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "CAP-OBSERVABILITY Operational telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Per-item metrics, freshness and cost, reaching gold so cost can be told apart from work."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: data"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "The platform measures the work done on each item, how fresh the data is, and what it costs, so you can tell a rise in spending from a rise in work."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "If a run crashes partway through an item, nothing is recorded unless the record was written first. And a process's status can say it's running when the work has actually hung."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Metrics for each item, whose status is crashed by default."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Heartbeats, and the cost of each task in gold."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-observability.md
msgid "Cap runs by wall time, but compare them by core time, because wall time changes with the topology."
msgstr ""

